Oilfield roller chains are essential power-transmission components used in drilling rigs, pump jacks and other heavy-duty equipment across upstream oil and gas operations. Manufactured from high-strength alloy steel, these chains are designed to withstand extreme loads, abrasive media and wide temperature variations while maintaining reliable torque transfer.
